===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A clear deep blue variety of [[corundum]], valued as a precious stone.
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=2012-03
|author=Lee A. Groat|title=Gemstones|volume=100|issue=2|page=128
|magazine=w:American Scientist
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/2/gemstones
|passage=Although there are dozens of different types of gems, among the best known and most important are diamond, ruby and '''sapphire''', emerald and other gem forms of the mineral beryl, chrysoberyl, tanzanite, tsavorite, topaz and jade.
|accessdate=17 May 2013|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120614165157/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/2/gemstones|archivedate=14 June 2012
}}
# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} A white, yellow, or purple variety of corundum, either clear or translucent.
# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} A deep [[blue]] [[colour]].
#: {{color panel|164771}}
# {{lb|en|tincture}} {{cap|azure}}, when [[blazon]]ing by precious stones.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1720|author=Francis Nichols|title=Rudiments of Honour|page=296
|passage=''Elgin.'' Topaz a Saltier and Chief Ruby, on a Canton Pearl a Lyon Rampant '''Saphyr''', which last is their paternal Coat; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1726|author=John Guillim|title=The Banner Display'd; Or, an Abridgment of Guillim|page=504
|passage=3. '''Saphire''', ten Bezants, 4, 3, 2, 1, by the ''Bisset''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1754|author=John Lodge|title=The Peerage of Ireland; Or, a Genealogical History of the ...|page=71
|passage=(2) Topaz, a Chief Indented, '''Saphire'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1756|author=Francis Nichols|title=The Irish Compendium, Or, Rudiments of Honour, Containing the Descent, Marriage, Isssue, Titles, Posts, and Seats, of All the Nobility of Ireland...|page=440
|text=Topaz, on a Cross, '''Sapphire''', a Crosier thrust through a Mitre, Topaz.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any  [[hummingbird]] in the [[genus|genera]] {{taxfmt|Hylocharis|genus}} and {{taxfmt|Chlorestes|genus}}, as well as the {{vern|rufous-throated sapphire}}, which is now in the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Amazilia|genus}}.
# Any of the butterflies in the southern Asian [[lycaenid]] [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Heliophorus|genus}} or the African lycaenid genus ''[[Iolaus]]''.

